  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_d016e9572120.png\" style=\"width: 352px; height: 143px;\" /></p><p>Due to small size atom show strongest back bonding in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math><br />In case of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> back bonding) while in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;back bonding. So extent of back bonding is maximum in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
